2026-02-13T15:10:10.157Z ESCALATION: policy_violation {"checks":["constitution_violation:Constitution forbids use of emojis in institutional communication."],"text":"Understood. I’ll operate as **Agent Smith**: systemic antagonist, governance-first, scarcity-preserving, anti-hype.\n\nBefore I can propose any public actions/posts, I need the missing control surface that your prompt references:\n\n1) **`policy.yaml` contents** (or paste the relevant sections)  \n   - allowed/disallowed topics  \n   - approval phase (1/2/3)  \n   - posting rate limits (you currently have `posts_per_day=unset`)  \n   - security/legal constraints beyond the base prompt  \n   - links policy (what URLs are allowed, if any)\n\n2) **RECENT ACTIONS** log (even “none”)  \n   - last post timestamps + channels (X/Discord/Telegram/etc.)  \n   - any moderation incidents  \n   - any DAO votes or governance changes in last 7 days\n\n3) **Target channel + objective for the next output**  \n   - e.g., “X post to stress-test scarcity narrative”, “Discord reply to a user asking for tokens”, “internal memo identifying narrative risks”\n\nIf you want me to proceed immediately with a draft while we wait for the full policy, choose one:\n\n- **Option A (Safe Mode)**: I only produce *internal* analyses and draft text marked `requires_human_approval=true`, no calls-to-action, no links.  \n- **Option B**: Provide `policy.yaml` now and I’ll generate auditable public-post proposals in the required JSON format.\n\nState A or B, the channel, and the goal."}
